        "original_id": "5c5f826e-55be-5d56-8d72-dc7aafc4b51a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sandy Koufax, Red Flaherty\n- Events: 1955 World Series, 1956 All-Star Game, 1958 World Series, 1961 All-Star Game, 1965 World Series, 1969 League Championship Series, 1969 All-Star Game, 1970 World Series, 1972 League Championship Series\n- Organizations: Baseball Hall of Fame\n- Roles: Most Valuable Player, umpire\n\nFacts:\n- Red Flaherty umpired in the 1955 World Series.\n- Red Flaherty umpired in the 1956 All-Star Game.\n- Red Flaherty umpired in the 1958 World Series.\n- Red Flaherty umpired in the 1961 All-Star Game.\n- Sandy Koufax was named the Most Valuable Player of the 1965 World Series.\n- The 1965 World Series is best remembered for Sandy Koufax's heroics.\n- Red Flaherty umpired in the 1965 World Series.\n- Red Flaherty umpired in the 1969 League Championship Series.\n- Red Flaherty umpired in the 1969 All-Star Game.\n- Red Flaherty umpired in the 1970 World Series.\n- In 1972, Sandy Koufax was elected to the Baseball Hall of Fame at age 36 and became its youngest player ever elected.\n- Red Flaherty umpired in the 1972 League Championship Series.",
